I remember exposing helper structs by accident. The tests ignored the return value from add_node, connect, add_ramp, register, and charge, but Rust still rejected public methods that returned private types. The clean fix was boring: mutating setup methods returned (), and only test-facing structs were public.

I remember the derive scar from the Ordo run. Public structs compared by tests derived Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, but I never put f64 fields inside those Eq structs. If a concept wanted a multiplier or cost, I stored integers or kept the float private and out of the compared struct.

